Both with the above repro and my recent simulation I get incorrect snippet expansion, probably because:

- like in my previous comment, `server_start_boundary = curstartbyte` which is `1` from the startCharacter
- at the end of trigger, just before calling `vim.fn.complete()` this value determines the column of `Context.cursor`:

https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/7088441de41c468e22dc5daffd377c00211ce45b/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/completion.lua#L555-L557

- then (`CompleteDone` callback) the buffer line is trimmed starting from that column (only `x` remains):

https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/7088441de41c468e22dc5daffd377c00211ce45b/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/completion.lua#L652-L659

so later that trivial snippet is expanded on wrong position.

Similarly: removing `Symbol` entry from completion results or adding a copy modified on the start column (see the repro at the end of my previous comment) hides that behavior.

~It suggests that `adjust_start_col()` may need fix.~

